    "Question #: 1": {
      "Title": "Exam MO-201 topic 1 question 1 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "SIMULATION -"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Instructions -"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Exam Environment -"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Exam Interface and Controls -"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The exam panel provides access to the project task(s). Each project has an associated file in which you will perform the project tasks."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "https://www.examtopics.com/assets/media/exam-media/03432/0000300001.jpg"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "1. Project file"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "2. Split bar"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "3. Exam panel"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "You can modify the exam interface to fit your needs in the following ways:"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 To increase or decrease the exam panel font size, press Ctrl+Plus or Ctrl+Minus."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 To change the height of the exam panel, drag the split bar between the project file and the exam panel."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "https://www.examtopics.com/assets/media/exam-media/03432/0000300005.jpg"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "To minimize the exam panel, click the Collapse Panel arrow"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "in the upper-left corner of the exam panel. The minimized exam panel displays the Expand"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "https://www.examtopics.com/assets/media/exam-media/03432/0000300004.png"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Panel button, the project number and name, the remaining time, and the Restart Project and Submit Project buttons. To move between tasks, you must expand the exam panel."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 To restore the interface to the default appearance, click the Restore button near the upper-right corner of the exam panel."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "https://www.examtopics.com/assets/media/exam-media/03432/0000400002.jpg"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "4. The Information bar at the top of the exam panel displays the current project and total number of projects, the remaining exam time, and the following commands:"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 Collapse Panel. Minimizes the exam panel to provide more space for the project file."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 Restart Project. Closes and reopens the current project file without saving your changes."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 Submit Project. Saves your changes, submits the project file, and moves to the next project."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 Calculator. A calculator is available in some exams. You are not required to use the calculator."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 Restore. Restores the size and position of the project file and exam panel to the defaults."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 Help. Displays information about the exam interface."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "5. The Content area displays the task tabs and the current task description."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "6. The Navigation area at the bottom of the exam panel contains the following commands."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 Previous Task/Next Task. Saves your response and moves to the previous or next task in the current project."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 Leave feedback after exam. Flags the task to indicate that you want to leave feedback about it after the exam."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 Mark for review. Flags the task to indicate that you want to return to it before you finish the exam."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 Mark as complete. Flags the task to indicate that you feel you have completed the task."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "In projects that contain multiple tasks, you can switch between tasks by clicking the task tab, Next Task button, or Previous Task button."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "End of the instructions."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "You are analyzing data about the number of visitors to U.S. National Parks."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Configure Excel so that you can edit content using Albanian as the editing language."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Do not make Albanian the default editing language. If you are prompted to restart Office, dismiss the prompt but do not restart Excel."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
